  "what_this_is": "Cell B4b-rep RESUME-RECOVERY (docs/readiness/2026-09-18-slurp-b4b-replicate-v2-resume-v1.md): the baseline of the resume-recovery attempt of cell B4b-rep, the request-identical same-roster replicate of cell B4b (module M4b, the date/time slot-contract revision, slot store v2) on the sealed dual-store anchor. It is configs/baseline/slurp-native-anchor-slot-store-v2-train-fold-a-replicate-v2.json byte for byte except ONE key: native_contact_fit.attempt_id, which mints a fresh native-fit attempt for the resumed flight. The FIT run id, both knowledge stores with their release and snapshot hashes, the arm speech-feature-query-native-tools, the policy phase-native-candidates-review-revise-v1, the full native episode with the Reviewer/Planner review loop on, the candidate supply contract, the Perception retrieval geometry, every instruction template, the phase_tools block, the scorers, the promoted EVO-FOLDS-V2 speech packets, the prepared-supply pin and BOTH WAVE R7 speech-feature identity strings are HELD at the aborted attempt's values, because a resume must not move a request byte: the 580 rows it keeps were produced under exactly these values and the 500 rows it flies must be produced under them too. Holding the two speech-feature identity strings is the deliberate opposite of the fresh-identity choice cell B4b-rep itself made against cell B4b (preregistration section 3.5); they ride the audited payload as ORG/CONTROL provenance, so a resumed manifest whose kept and flown rows disagreed about them would be internally inconsistent for no gain. The fresh FIT attempt id is required by the RUNTIME, not chosen: core.preparation_fit.build_native_contact_fit_gate writes one request-fit receipt per realized contact to prepared/<fit run>/<fit attempt>/<sha256 of sample_id + agent_contact_id>.request-fit.json and refuses a path that already exists (\"native contact fit identity already has contact or result evidence\"), and agent_contact_id is the deterministic <program>:<phase>:<iteration>:<sample id>. All four partial rows of the aborted attempt (slurp:train:008363, slurp:train:008450, slurp:train:008472, slurp:train:008505) already carry perception:0 and solver:0 receipts under the aborted fit attempt, so re-flying them under that attempt would refuse at the first contact; the fit root is namespaced by run AND attempt, so a fresh attempt id under the SAME fit run id is the minimum change that clears it and keeps the run's exposure accounting on its existing two rows. The FIT contact_cap stays 47,520 = 1,080 rows x 11 contacts x (1 speech packet + 3 endpoints), because the gate derives the required cap from the whole registered roster and not from the flown subset. None of this reaches a rendered request byte: native contact-fit receipts are namespaced by the FIT run and attempt id, and the preregistration's section 3.1 scan found 0 hits of the run-id and attempt-id prefixes in 12,960 rendered envelopes.",
